{"author":{"id":"686d9350e5e426946f54ca7a73ceeef9fd8682b44ea6617ce58187e451c43768"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792313459,"nonce":"pB4DvxkmK/N/HmFhht+/6j50TdA=","title":"The web build ships in the Haxelib ZIP and a wasm build stages it","message":"The wasm build was a separate release zip, `hlwgpu-wasm-ash.zip`, and a program built for a page had to collect its files by hand. A build defined `wasm` with `-lib hlwgpu` should have them beside its output without a Rust toolchain, as a desktop build has its hdll.\n\n**Done**\n\n- `scripts/package_haxelib.py --web \u003cdirectory\u003e` puts xgpu.wasm, gpu.mjs, gpu-worker.mjs, gpu-agent.mjs and hlwgpu.js in the ZIP under `web/`, and stops the release when one is missing; the release workflow passes the wasm job's artifact.\n- `hlwgpu.macro.NativeInstall` copies them beside the output of a build defined `wasm`, in place of the host library. `-D hlwgpu_web=\u003cdirectory\u003e` names another directory, for a checkout whose web build is in `target`.\n\n**Context**\n\nashui's page build stages its own page and `blinc_abi.wasm`; with these, a web build of an app needs no step but the Haxe compile and `ash --build`.","files":null}]}